inside a project. You can, of course, also

3
00:00:06,277 --> 00:00:07,481
create those tasks

4
00:00:08,219 --> 00:00:10,322
completely disconnected from a project.

5
00:00:10,868 --> 00:00:13,533
For this, we go back to the Scheduled menu

6
00:00:14,384 --> 00:00:15,957
and create a task in here,

7
00:00:16,551 --> 00:00:17,820
or alternatively,

8
00:00:18,574 --> 00:00:20,292
we start a new session

9
00:00:21,046 --> 00:00:23,968
and select a new folder, and now I have a

10
00:00:23,968 --> 00:00:27,404
Scheduled Tasks folder, and in here, with my

11
00:00:27,404 --> 00:00:30,086
slash command, I can now refer to the

12
00:00:30,391 --> 00:00:31,276
schedule skill.

13
00:00:31,823 --> 00:00:33,996
And here I can just paste the task that

14
00:00:33,996 --> 00:00:36,055
should be created because the skill knows

15
00:00:36,088 --> 00:00:38,972
how to manage this task creation process. So

16
00:00:38,972 --> 00:00:40,570
all we gotta do is we gotta run this.

17
00:00:41,393 --> 00:00:44,507
Now it starts up the task creation process.

18
00:00:45,184 --> 00:00:47,862
We want to run this daily at 7 AM.

19
00:00:48,395 --> 00:00:49,779
Now we want to schedule this.

20
00:00:52,413 --> 00:00:53,279
And now we are done.

21
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:57,931
So as you saw, we just added the /schedule

22
00:00:57,996 --> 00:01:00,156
command to work with that skill,

23
00:01:00,685 --> 00:01:03,795
we added the actual task description, and

24
00:01:03,811 --> 00:01:05,927
now Claude managed everything for us.

25
00:01:06,697 --> 00:01:09,310
And if we go back to our scheduled menu, you

26
00:01:09,342 --> 00:01:12,067
can now find this task right here.

27
00:01:12,869 --> 00:01:15,338
Now, if we select the task, you can see it

28
00:01:15,338 --> 00:01:19,121
is not related to a project here. It is just

29
00:01:19,121 --> 00:01:21,606
referring to a specific folder. So the

30
00:01:21,606 --> 00:01:24,011
project folder we actually used in a

31
00:01:24,011 --> 00:01:26,336
specific session, which I also recommend

32
00:01:26,336 --> 00:01:28,484
because you always need some kind of output

33
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:30,740
folder for your results. So you should

34
00:01:30,757 --> 00:01:33,471
always select a folder if you're not working

35
00:01:33,729 --> 00:01:34,828
on a project here.

36
00:01:36,404 --> 00:01:38,072
And now we can either let it run

37
00:01:38,331 --> 00:01:38,963
automatically

38
00:01:39,627 --> 00:01:41,992
or we can let it run manually if you want

39
00:01:41,992 --> 00:01:43,985
to. Now the interesting thing is if I run

40
00:01:44,098 --> 00:01:44,940
this task now,

41
00:01:47,222 --> 00:01:49,653
it should result in an error because our

42
00:01:49,702 --> 00:01:52,165
Gmail connector is not activated.

43
00:01:52,696 --> 00:01:55,579
So let's see what the result was of this

44
00:01:55,579 --> 00:01:58,856
task. Gmail isn't connected, so this is not

45
00:01:58,856 --> 00:02:01,266
working. And if we check our morning brief

46
00:02:01,266 --> 00:02:03,676
here, yeah, we get the information that we

47
00:02:03,676 --> 00:02:04,222
have to run

48
00:02:04,816 --> 00:02:07,628
or add this connector to run this task

49
00:02:07,628 --> 00:02:08,270
successfully.

50
00:02:08,833 --> 00:02:09,283
And by the way,

51
00:02:10,423 --> 00:02:12,496
if we go to scheduled once again

52
00:02:13,315 --> 00:02:16,464
and rerun our morning brief schedule here,

53
00:02:17,331 --> 00:02:20,094
it is added to the history. So you can see

54
00:02:20,625 --> 00:02:23,099
all the iterations of that specific task.

55
00:02:23,452 --> 00:02:24,896
When you let it run, whether it was

56
00:02:24,896 --> 00:02:26,933
successful or not. You can see all that here

57
00:02:27,062 --> 00:02:29,581
in this history. And now if you select the

58
00:02:29,709 --> 00:02:32,645
Monday status snapshot, you are directly

59
00:02:32,902 --> 00:02:35,405
redirected to the actual session, to the

60
00:02:35,629 --> 00:02:36,415
chat interface.

61
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:39,351
But for the morning brief, you are

62
00:02:39,480 --> 00:02:40,474
redirected to the,

63
00:02:41,261 --> 00:02:43,073
to the task itself, because

64
00:02:43,812 --> 00:02:46,330
in the session then you can switch between

65
00:02:46,379 --> 00:02:49,074
the different times when you ran this

66
00:02:49,122 --> 00:02:50,087
scheduled task.

67
00:02:50,634 --> 00:02:52,740
So this means you have everything organized.

68
00:02:53,222 --> 00:02:56,035
If you run the same task again and again, it

69
00:02:56,099 --> 00:02:58,656
doesn't create a new session. It all remains

70
00:02:58,768 --> 00:03:00,858
in that one session you started where you

71
00:03:00,858 --> 00:03:02,932
can switch between the different points in

72
00:03:02,932 --> 00:03:05,054
time when you ran this task.
